1
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:13,880
(This story is entirely fictional)

2
00:00:14,039 --> 00:00:15,919
We used to write to each other.

3
00:00:16,920 --> 00:00:18,320
Those were good times, right?

4
00:00:19,920 --> 00:00:20,879
It wasn't happiness.

5
00:00:22,320 --> 00:00:23,760
It was my only support

6
00:00:24,719 --> 00:00:25,879
after my dad died.

7
00:00:29,719 --> 00:00:33,000
(Based on novel Doctor Qin: Executer)
Actually, I asked you out that night

8
00:00:33,960 --> 00:00:35,280
to confess my feelings.

9
00:00:40,120 --> 00:00:44,120
(Ten years ago)

10
00:00:47,920 --> 00:00:48,719
Qin,

11
00:00:49,039 --> 00:00:50,280
it's raining this hard.

12
00:00:50,679 --> 00:00:51,920
Looks like your plans are shot.

13
00:00:52,119 --> 00:00:53,679
Why not try another way to confess?

14
00:00:53,799 --> 00:00:55,280
Just write her a love letter,

15
00:00:55,280 --> 00:00:56,399
then tuck a flower petal inside.

16
00:00:56,399 --> 00:00:57,520
I'll make sure it gets to her!

17
00:00:59,679 --> 00:01:00,759
It's just a passing shower

18
00:01:00,799 --> 00:01:01,799
with southerly winds at Force 5.

19
00:01:02,159 --> 00:01:03,719
The rain clouds have almost blown away.

20
00:01:03,840 --> 00:01:05,200
It'll definitely clear up after eight.

21
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:06,920
Awesome!

22
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:08,760
(Fireworks)

23
00:01:13,079 --> 00:01:13,879
Qin,

24
00:01:14,040 --> 00:01:15,560
I won't question

25
00:01:15,640 --> 00:01:16,480
your weather forecast.

26
00:01:16,640 --> 00:01:18,359
But when it comes to girls,

27
00:01:18,560 --> 00:01:19,760
you still have a lot to learn.

28
00:01:22,560 --> 00:01:24,000
Your dad's not around
to keep tabs on you,

29
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:25,599
but I need to get home now.

30
00:01:25,719 --> 00:01:26,519
Any later

31
00:01:26,519 --> 00:01:27,799
and my dad will kill me!

32
00:01:29,120 --> 00:01:31,000
Jin Keke isn't coming tonight.

33
00:01:32,840 --> 00:01:33,640
Light it.

34
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:54,920
(That night,)

35
00:01:56,519 --> 00:01:57,599
(I kept waiting for you.)

36
00:01:57,680 --> 00:01:59,680
(Longfan University Affiliated
High School Dropout Certificate)

37
00:02:06,680 --> 00:02:08,199
(You left without saying a word.)

38
00:02:09,280 --> 00:02:10,319
(I was pretty upset.)

39
00:02:12,840 --> 00:02:13,639
(Tell me...)

40
00:02:14,639 --> 00:02:16,479
(If all that had never happened,)

41
00:02:18,039 --> 00:02:19,000
(would we...)

42
00:02:39,840 --> 00:02:40,639
Officer Qin.

43
00:02:43,840 --> 00:02:44,879
You'd better head back now.

44
00:02:45,240 --> 00:02:47,919
You've got cases to solve tomorrow.

45
00:02:53,840 --> 00:02:57,840
=Doctor Qin: Executer=
=Episode 15=

46
00:02:58,159 --> 00:03:00,319
All of Qiao Shengchan's
social connections

47
00:03:00,319 --> 00:03:01,560
have been cut off.

48
00:03:01,840 --> 00:03:04,879
Liu Sanhao, the only one
who knew his family, is dead too.

49
00:03:05,120 --> 00:03:07,319
Now he's vanished completely.

50
00:03:07,719 --> 00:03:09,120
(Notes)
Unless there's a special reason,

51
00:03:09,280 --> 00:03:10,120
Qiao Shengchan,

52
00:03:10,520 --> 00:03:12,879
a well-behaved ex-con,

53
00:03:12,919 --> 00:03:13,960
has no need to hide.

54
00:03:14,319 --> 00:03:17,759
Su Shi, Le Tianyi,
Liu Sanhao, Zhang Xiaodong...

55
00:03:17,960 --> 00:03:19,960
and now Qiao Shengchan is missing too.

56
00:03:20,080 --> 00:03:21,879
(Notes)
Maybe the so-called Executer

57
00:03:22,759 --> 00:03:24,319
has a hit list?

58
00:03:24,319 --> 00:03:25,560
We're now racing

59
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:26,680
against a ghost

60
00:03:26,680 --> 00:03:28,360
we can't even see.

61
00:03:28,360 --> 00:03:28,759
(Retribution has come.
Every sin will be paid for.)

62
00:03:28,759 --> 00:03:30,400
They have the upper hand on everything:

63
00:03:30,840 --> 00:03:33,159
the time, the place, and the target.

64
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:34,800
And we're

65
00:03:35,319 --> 00:03:36,680
always one step behind.

66
00:03:43,680 --> 00:03:48,160
(Weiyou Mart)

67
00:03:50,800 --> 00:03:51,879
Liu Sanhao is dead.

68
00:03:52,439 --> 00:03:53,240
What?

69
00:03:53,680 --> 00:03:55,400
You already told me that.

70
00:03:59,560 --> 00:04:00,400
But we found out

71
00:04:01,800 --> 00:04:02,879
your father's death

72
00:04:04,080 --> 00:04:05,520
was connected to Liu Sanhao.

73
00:04:07,199 --> 00:04:08,159
Do you think

74
00:04:08,400 --> 00:04:09,919
I have a motive to kill him?

75
00:04:10,599 --> 00:04:12,080
Are you investigating me now?

76
00:04:15,840 --> 00:04:16,639
That's right.

77
00:04:17,040 --> 00:04:18,120
I hated him.

78
00:04:18,519 --> 00:04:20,000
I dreamed of seeing him dead.

79
00:04:20,800 --> 00:04:21,680
But, Qin Ming,

80
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:24,160
my dad wasn't the only one
driven to death

81
00:04:24,160 --> 00:04:25,519
by Liu's loan shark debts.

82
00:04:26,319 --> 00:04:28,160
Those who want him dead

83
00:04:28,160 --> 00:04:30,879
could line up around the block.

84
00:04:31,160 --> 00:04:32,160
Who am I to them?

85
00:04:34,079 --> 00:04:34,879
Well,

86
00:04:36,439 --> 00:04:38,920
if people cheered over his death,

87
00:04:39,199 --> 00:04:40,199
let me tell you this:

88
00:04:40,920 --> 00:04:42,519
I'd definitely be one of them.

89
00:04:43,639 --> 00:04:44,519
Besides,

90
00:04:44,920 --> 00:04:46,160
my dad died a long time ago.

91
00:04:46,519 --> 00:04:47,800
He's nothing but ashes now.

92
00:04:48,720 --> 00:04:50,120
But I still have to live.

93
00:04:51,040 --> 00:04:51,839
Revenge?

94
00:04:52,360 --> 00:04:54,360
That's the kind of thing
you see in movies.

95
00:04:54,800 --> 00:04:55,879
Sounds great,

96
00:04:56,920 --> 00:04:58,600
but for a nobody like me,

97
00:05:00,120 --> 00:05:01,120
I don't have the ability,

98
00:05:01,560 --> 00:05:02,720
or the energy for it.

99
00:05:08,600 --> 00:05:09,040
(Weiyou Mart)

100
00:05:09,040 --> 00:05:09,839
The last skewer.

101
00:05:15,199 --> 00:05:17,120
If we lose touch again,

102
00:05:19,040 --> 00:05:20,879
would you still wait this long
to find me?

103
00:05:28,720 --> 00:05:33,920
(Weiyou Mart)

104
00:05:33,920 --> 00:05:34,720
Hello, Han.

105
00:05:39,000 --> 00:05:40,879
There are quite a few in town

106
00:05:41,839 --> 00:05:42,720
who won't be sleeping tonight.

107
00:05:43,519 --> 00:05:44,279
Got it.

108
00:05:45,839 --> 00:05:46,639
Keke,

109
00:05:47,240 --> 00:05:48,720
I have to go back for a meeting.

110
00:05:49,439 --> 00:05:50,519
I'll come back and pick you up.

111
00:05:57,680 --> 00:05:58,480
Qin Ming,

112
00:06:00,560 --> 00:06:02,079
I'm not waiting for you this time.

113
00:06:04,759 --> 00:06:06,199
We found the drone fragments,

114
00:06:06,199 --> 00:06:08,079
but there's only so much footage

115
00:06:08,160 --> 00:06:09,319
we can recover.

116
00:06:11,279 --> 00:06:12,600
This is the first recovered segment.

117
00:06:23,199 --> 00:06:25,519
The person's decisive and strong.

118
00:06:26,399 --> 00:06:27,879
They likely have experience
with violent crimes.

119
00:06:31,800 --> 00:06:32,720
There's another accomplice!

120
00:06:48,440 --> 00:06:49,520
(Ah!)

121
00:06:49,560 --> 00:06:50,360
(Help!)

122
00:06:59,759 --> 00:07:01,639
That's all the footage we recovered.

123
00:07:01,639 --> 00:07:03,079
Under our tight surveillance,

124
00:07:03,079 --> 00:07:04,439
how could the killers commit the murder

125
00:07:04,439 --> 00:07:05,720
on the rooftop?

126
00:07:05,920 --> 00:07:07,759
We searched the entire building,

127
00:07:07,759 --> 00:07:09,519
but found no one suspicious.

128
00:07:09,680 --> 00:07:11,240
We must've missed something.

129
00:07:11,279 --> 00:07:12,160
I just thought of something.

130
00:07:12,160 --> 00:07:13,360
There was a case before

131
00:07:13,720 --> 00:07:15,079
where the crime scene
was in Building One.

132
00:07:15,560 --> 00:07:17,519
We searched the entire building
and came up empty-handed.

133
00:07:18,000 --> 00:07:19,480
Finally, we realized
the killer had accessed there

134
00:07:19,480 --> 00:07:20,480
through Building Two.

135
00:07:20,480 --> 00:07:21,680
How did they get there?

136
00:07:21,759 --> 00:07:23,040
The rooftops are connected.

137
00:07:23,560 --> 00:07:24,839
Liang, we found something.

138
00:07:25,319 --> 00:07:27,120
The tenant of Unit 1705 next building

139
00:07:27,120 --> 00:07:27,959
is Qiao Shengchan.

140
00:07:28,399 --> 00:07:29,879
Move! Go get him!

141
00:07:37,840 --> 00:07:41,520
(Retribution has come.
Every sin will be paid for.)

142
00:07:53,480 --> 00:07:54,160
Keke!

143
00:07:54,160 --> 00:07:55,839
Welcome.

144
00:07:58,040 --> 00:07:58,920
Where's Jin Keke?

145
00:07:59,560 --> 00:08:00,720
Who's Jin Keke?

146
00:08:03,759 --> 00:08:05,879
The manager called me
to cover the shift.

147
00:08:05,879 --> 00:08:07,519
I don't know who you're talking about.

148
00:08:12,879 --> 00:08:13,879
(You must be tired too.)

149
00:08:14,000 --> 00:08:15,240
(We're all tired.)

150
00:08:17,560 --> 00:08:20,279
(Do you think
I have a motive to kill him?)

151
00:08:20,959 --> 00:08:22,439
(Are you investigating me now?)

152
00:08:26,240 --> 00:08:27,160
(There's another accomplice!)

153
00:08:33,279 --> 00:08:34,080
(Shengchan!)

154
00:08:34,879 --> 00:08:35,559
(Buddy.)

155
00:08:35,679 --> 00:08:36,440
Bro.

156
00:08:38,399 --> 00:08:39,360
Nine years.

157
00:08:40,200 --> 00:08:41,759
The best nine years of my life

158
00:08:41,759 --> 00:08:43,120
are going to be wasted here.

159
00:08:43,360 --> 00:08:44,720
What nonsense!

160
00:08:45,200 --> 00:08:45,960
How can you say

161
00:08:45,960 --> 00:08:48,080
they're the best nine years?

162
00:08:48,360 --> 00:08:49,720
Once you get out,

163
00:08:49,840 --> 00:08:51,759
the good years will just be starting.

164
00:08:51,759 --> 00:08:53,399
But my wife and my mom...

165
00:08:53,639 --> 00:08:54,799
With no man at home,

166
00:08:54,799 --> 00:08:56,320
they'll just get bullied.

167
00:08:56,320 --> 00:08:57,120
Enough.

168
00:08:57,480 --> 00:08:58,639
Look at you,

169
00:08:58,639 --> 00:08:59,759
getting all sentimental.

170
00:08:59,759 --> 00:09:02,399
Bro, I've worked for you
all these years.

171
00:09:02,919 --> 00:09:03,480
I mean,

172
00:09:03,480 --> 00:09:04,799
you can't just abandon them.

173
00:09:04,799 --> 00:09:05,720
Since you call me your brother,

174
00:09:05,720 --> 00:09:06,840
how could I abandon them?

175
00:09:07,240 --> 00:09:09,240
How could I let them be mistreated?

176
00:09:09,240 --> 00:09:09,960
From now on,

177
00:09:11,720 --> 00:09:12,919
your mother

178
00:09:13,600 --> 00:09:14,679
will be like my own mom,

179
00:09:15,480 --> 00:09:17,559
and your wife will be...

180
00:09:19,679 --> 00:09:20,559
like my own sister.

181
00:09:20,919 --> 00:09:21,519
All right?

182
00:09:23,000 --> 00:09:24,000
Buddy, you...

183
00:09:24,000 --> 00:09:25,559
I... I was wrong.

184
00:09:25,559 --> 00:09:26,320
Please let me go.

185
00:09:26,320 --> 00:09:26,840
I'm begging you!

186
00:09:26,840 --> 00:09:27,320
I was wrong!

187
00:09:27,559 --> 00:09:28,039
I was wrong!

188
00:09:28,039 --> 00:09:29,960
You've harmed too many people.

189
00:09:30,559 --> 00:09:32,360
Do you remember Jin Qingshan?

190
00:09:33,399 --> 00:09:34,960
He borrowed 80,000 from you.

191
00:09:35,480 --> 00:09:36,519
He paid for three years,

192
00:09:37,440 --> 00:09:38,639
100,000 a year,

193
00:09:38,639 --> 00:09:40,000
and still owed you 500,000.

194
00:09:40,480 --> 00:09:42,320
You forced his daughter

195
00:09:42,840 --> 00:09:44,759
to work for Zhang Xiaodong

196
00:09:45,200 --> 00:09:47,360
with her father's life.

197
00:09:47,639 --> 00:09:49,440
You knew that once she was there,

198
00:09:49,559 --> 00:09:50,559
she'd have to endure

199
00:09:50,559 --> 00:09:52,039
the most desperate time of her life,

200
00:09:52,039 --> 00:09:52,759
didn't you?

201
00:09:52,799 --> 00:09:55,360
I... I was just the middleman!

202
00:09:55,360 --> 00:09:56,399
He was the sick one.

203
00:09:56,399 --> 00:09:58,639
He liked watching girls
do whatever he said.

204
00:09:58,759 --> 00:10:00,159
I only found girls for him.

205
00:10:00,720 --> 00:10:01,919
I never touched them.

206
00:10:02,559 --> 00:10:03,840
I really didn't touch them.

207
00:10:03,919 --> 00:10:05,120
I never touched them...

208
00:10:05,120 --> 00:10:06,320
I... I'm sorry about your dad.

209
00:10:06,759 --> 00:10:07,879
Shengchan, I'm sorry!

210
00:10:07,879 --> 00:10:10,559
What do you want from me?

211
00:10:10,559 --> 00:10:12,600
I'm begging you!

212
00:10:12,600 --> 00:10:13,559
I'm begging you!

213
00:10:13,759 --> 00:10:14,759
I'm begging you!

214
00:10:14,759 --> 00:10:15,639
Please...

215
00:10:19,360 --> 00:10:22,639
When Jin Qingshan died, do you know

216
00:10:24,559 --> 00:10:26,320
what was troubling his daughter?

217
00:10:26,879 --> 00:10:28,120
No... I don't know.

218
00:10:28,440 --> 00:10:29,360
She was thinking,

219
00:10:29,720 --> 00:10:30,600
after she'd already worked

220
00:10:30,600 --> 00:10:32,039
for Zhang Xiaodong,

221
00:10:32,039 --> 00:10:33,759
and done all those disgusting things,

222
00:10:33,759 --> 00:10:35,559
why her father still had to die!

223
00:11:01,840 --> 00:11:05,280
(Innovate and Renew)

224
00:11:06,240 --> 00:11:07,320
She couldn't figure it out.

225
00:11:09,639 --> 00:11:10,440
(Xiaoxue...)

226
00:11:11,519 --> 00:11:12,399
(I'm sorry.)

227
00:11:17,039 --> 00:11:17,960
Some people

228
00:11:19,840 --> 00:11:21,759
don't deserve to be called human.

229
00:11:45,279 --> 00:11:46,080
Dad...

230
00:11:46,799 --> 00:11:48,000
Dad!

231
00:12:15,919 --> 00:12:16,720
(Miss,)

232
00:12:16,759 --> 00:12:17,600
(are you okay?)

233
00:12:20,720 --> 00:12:21,600
I'm fine.

234
00:12:23,960 --> 00:12:24,879
I'm fine.

235
00:12:29,000 --> 00:12:29,799
Dad...

236
00:12:34,240 --> 00:12:35,679
I've avenged you.

237
00:12:59,200 --> 00:13:01,960
(Police)

238
00:13:06,639 --> 00:13:07,600
That felt good!

239
00:13:12,799 --> 00:13:14,600
Miss, are you okay?

240
00:13:18,480 --> 00:13:19,639
When are we leaving?

241
00:13:21,759 --> 00:13:23,399
There's one more important thing.

242
00:13:25,039 --> 00:13:26,399
I knew it.

243
00:13:26,420 --> 00:13:26,840
Hey,

244
00:13:27,279 --> 00:13:28,080
I've got your back.

245
00:13:32,559 --> 00:13:33,960
Whatever I want to do,

246
00:13:35,320 --> 00:13:36,639
you'll help me, right?

247
00:13:37,720 --> 00:13:39,600
I've got nothing left to lose.

248
00:13:40,039 --> 00:13:41,200
If I can help you

249
00:13:41,240 --> 00:13:42,279
complete the things

250
00:13:42,320 --> 00:13:43,759
on your wish list,

251
00:13:44,320 --> 00:13:45,399
that counts as atonement.

252
00:13:59,639 --> 00:14:00,759
When are we leaving?

253
00:14:31,840 --> 00:14:33,520
(1705)

254
00:14:36,600 --> 00:14:38,400
(1706)

255
00:15:03,559 --> 00:15:04,480
(It's you.)

256
00:15:10,759 --> 00:15:12,559
Judging by how moldy the food is,

257
00:15:12,559 --> 00:15:14,279
he left about two days ago.

258
00:15:14,840 --> 00:15:15,559
Liang,

259
00:15:15,559 --> 00:15:17,200
we traced the drone's registration.

260
00:15:17,559 --> 00:15:18,360
Who is it?

261
00:15:18,720 --> 00:15:19,679
Su Qingchen.

262
00:15:19,960 --> 00:15:20,840
Su Qingchen?

263
00:15:22,240 --> 00:15:23,600
The drone was registered

264
00:15:23,720 --> 00:15:25,360
in a victim's name?

265
00:15:25,440 --> 00:15:26,960
Has Su Qingchen's family

266
00:15:26,960 --> 00:15:28,200
had any large deposits recently?

267
00:15:28,200 --> 00:15:29,559
Yes. I was about to tell you.

268
00:15:29,799 --> 00:15:31,600
Three days ago,

269
00:15:31,600 --> 00:15:33,759
her father deposited $50,000 in one go.

270
00:15:40,919 --> 00:15:43,080
I didn't have the courage
to tell you before.

271
00:15:43,360 --> 00:15:45,000
They avenged us

272
00:15:45,720 --> 00:15:47,200
and gave me life-saving money.

273
00:15:47,600 --> 00:15:48,759
They're not a bad person.

274
00:15:48,759 --> 00:15:51,679
The drone was registered under her name,

275
00:15:52,000 --> 00:15:53,000
but I operated it.

276
00:15:53,000 --> 00:15:53,960
She was innocent.

277
00:15:54,200 --> 00:15:55,240
I'll go with you.

278
00:15:55,759 --> 00:15:56,600
Mr. Su,

279
00:15:56,679 --> 00:15:59,200
For now,
we're not calling you accomplices.

280
00:15:59,279 --> 00:16:00,600
We'll find out the truth.

281
00:16:00,679 --> 00:16:01,879
We won't unfairly blame you.

282
00:16:05,640 --> 00:16:06,000
(Evidence Packaging Bag)

283
00:16:07,040 --> 00:16:11,320
(Get treatment, live well.)

284
00:16:13,040 --> 00:16:17,840
♪Moonlight soaks the withered sunflower♪

285
00:16:19,080 --> 00:16:20,279
That felt great!

286
00:16:21,480 --> 00:16:23,399
Did you see how pathetic Liu Sanhao was?

287
00:16:23,440 --> 00:16:25,399
Begging for mercy, worse off than a dog.

288
00:16:27,080 --> 00:16:28,679
After we pull off this last job,

289
00:16:29,399 --> 00:16:30,360
I'll take you to a place

290
00:16:30,360 --> 00:16:31,759
where no one can find us.

291
00:16:32,159 --> 00:16:32,960
By then,

292
00:16:33,720 --> 00:16:35,159
you'll be my own sister.

293
00:16:35,879 --> 00:16:37,000
For the rest of my life,

294
00:16:37,120 --> 00:16:38,200
I'll work like a horse for you

295
00:16:38,519 --> 00:16:39,320
and protect you!

296
00:16:44,960 --> 00:16:45,799
Where will we go?

297
00:16:46,360 --> 00:16:47,279
Anywhere.

298
00:16:47,799 --> 00:16:48,639
You decide.

299
00:16:52,399 --> 00:16:53,600
Then let's go to a place

300
00:16:55,080 --> 00:16:56,039
where all grudges

301
00:16:56,279 --> 00:16:57,840
can be wiped clean.

302
00:16:57,840 --> 00:17:02,640
♪The sunflower bows, reciting names♪

303
00:17:03,400 --> 00:17:07,200
♪Each petal is a solemn phrase♪

304
00:17:08,880 --> 00:17:10,240
♪And moonlight♪

305
00:17:10,360 --> 00:17:12,800
♪Forever fair♪

306
00:17:13,360 --> 00:17:14,840
♪Lights up crime and punishment♪

307
00:17:18,760 --> 00:17:22,840
♪Lights up crime and punishment♪

308
00:17:22,840 --> 00:17:27,960
♪Lights up crime and punishment♪

309
00:17:35,080 --> 00:17:39,310
♪Sunset washes over the old wall♪

310
00:17:39,840 --> 00:17:44,180
♪Milk tea cools on the stone steps♪

311
00:17:44,180 --> 00:17:48,180
♪Sea wind tugs at your sleeve♪

312
00:17:48,670 --> 00:17:52,530
♪Unspoken words just flee and fade♪

313
00:18:01,510 --> 00:18:05,420
♪The marks on the desk
have faded yellow♪

314
00:18:05,420 --> 00:18:08,400
♪I turned around, and a gunshot rang out♪

315
00:18:08,920 --> 00:18:12,540
♪No one can truly feel another's pain♪

316
00:18:12,540 --> 00:18:16,770
♪The wind is cold,
a fading shadow sways♪

317
00:18:16,770 --> 00:18:21,490
♪Tonight, I don't care
about the universe♪

318
00:18:21,490 --> 00:18:25,640
♪I only want to see this through
with you♪

319
00:18:26,510 --> 00:18:30,290
♪A bullet pierces the spring night♪

320
00:18:30,290 --> 00:18:34,380
♪You sink into the vast crowd♪

321
00:18:43,340 --> 00:18:47,550
♪Years later, when we meet again♪

322
00:18:47,550 --> 00:18:51,890
♪Don't mention this moonlit night♪

323
00:18:51,890 --> 00:18:55,660
♪The waves smooth
two lines of footprints♪

324
00:18:55,660 --> 00:18:58,560
♪Half a cup of sweetness
sinks into the sand♪

325
00:18:58,560 --> 00:19:03,350
♪Tonight, I don't care
about the universe♪

326
00:19:03,350 --> 00:19:08,000
♪I only want to see this through
with you♪

327
00:19:08,000 --> 00:19:10,260
♪Wind back to shore,
clouds back to hills♪

328
00:19:10,260 --> 00:19:12,400
♪We stop here in this night♪

329
00:19:12,400 --> 00:19:16,820
♪This is the past, the only,
the last look back♪

330
00:19:16,820 --> 00:19:22,800
♪One gunshot echoes through half a life♪

331
00:19:25,220 --> 00:19:31,560
♪One gunshot echoes through half a life♪

332
00:19:43,080 --> 00:19:50,010
♪One gunshot echoes through half a life♪

333
